{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792577180,"nonce":"ZzXrL4c4LPP6Ru2I1GcekZroyp8=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/36","origin":"github","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:id":"I_kwDOUJip488AAAABYyb3ew","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:labels":"","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:number":"36","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:status":"open","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:text":"e1d065e872703600f93c4805f7a86ee3d324de9fe3bc3c68ecb171a020d6f383","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:title":"co2: check what filters on the bug/feat labels before kind-types","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/36"},"title":"co2: check what filters on the bug/feat labels before kind-types","message":"Raised by the amended ADR 0001 (issue-metadata-map, 2026-10-21). With native-fields, a kind held as the GitHub Issue Type is no longer a label on GitHub. Once co2's bridges set `kind-types = bug=Bug,feat=Feature`, the flat `bug` and `feat` labels come off every co2 issue that holds the type. Anything that filters on those labels would then silently stop matching: Project 40's automations, saved searches, the issue templates' auto-labels, and people's bookmarks.\n\nBefore any co2 sync sets `kind-types`:\n- [ ] List what filters on `bug`/`feat` in co2, read only: Project 40's workflows and views, the repository's workflows, saved searches. Never write to co2 or Project 40.\n- [ ] Then decide:\n  - (a) move those filters to `type:Bug`/`type:Feature`. GitHub Projects can filter and group on the Issue Type, since `ProjectV2FieldType` has `ISSUE_TYPE`.\n  - (b) a third mode in the fork, e.g. `kinds = both`, that keeps the label beside the type. That is ADR 0001's original rule, and it needs design: which side wins when they disagree.\n  - (c) leave co2 without `kind-types`. Its kinds then stay flat labels, and types come in as `kind:bug` and so on beside them.","files":null}]}